2026-09-23 — B04 reference-limit accounting, not a new campaign.
Fixed linux/arm64, network none, evo-flight-lab:sealed:
  image 2c23684c9cc5ef5899073b59844fa47cc3c1d894f2316e21f25d5d85be5a10e2
  GCC 14.2.0-19; Debian Clang 19.1.7; GNU11; O0/O2; 10 s per execution.
  EvoCC ae75daf20819c4f27fd041c0164d4a085dbc2008af019c0e1c0266275946c142

HVA reduction: hva-varargs-reference.c, worker compiled without HVA_DRIVER;
driver compiled separately with -DHVA_DRIVER (-DHVA_TRACE for printed values).
The aggregate contains two 8-byte integer vectors. One/four arguments exercise
the SIMD save area; five crosses to the stack; eight named vector arguments
force the whole anonymous pair onto the stack. Expected: 11 / 44 / 55 / 11.

                            one   four  five  stacked   exit
GCC O0                       11     44    55       11      0
GCC O2                        0      0    11       11      1
Clang O0                     11     44    55       11      0
Clang O2                     11     44    55       11      0
GCC O2 -fno-strict-aliasing   11     44    55       11      0

The GCC O2 worker itself warns that its compiler-generated ha.3 may be
uninitialized. In read_pairs, .L7 is the register-argument path: it increments
the iteration and adds x4, initialized to zero, without loading an argument.
The stack path does load offsets 0/14 and produces the expected result.
Disabling tree-sra, tree-dce or tree-fre separately does not fix the result;
disabling strict aliasing does. This isolates the failing reference path and
an optimization dependency, not a proved GCC internal pass/bug-number diagnosis.
The C source does not alias incompatible objects: the caller and va_arg use
the identical aggregate type. No workaround flag changes the accepted O2 lane.

EvoCC/EvoCC plus all four reference callers/EvoCC callee and EvoCC caller/
GCC O0, Clang O0/O2 callee: 8/8 PASS. EvoCC caller/GCC O2 callee: exit 1,
matching the broken GCC self-control; ORACLE_UNUSABLE, never PASS.
Original integer-vector-varargs-{worker,driver}.c replays unchanged:
same eight usable pairs PASS; EvoCC caller/GCC O2 callee and GCC O2 self-control
both exit 2. Existing vector_variadic_values_keep_the_simd_argument_class Rust
regression passes both interpreters and assembly generation. No ABI change.
Sub-8-byte vector ABI disagreement remains the separate L06 task.

Three original torture sources, hashes checked against the disposition table:
  pr39228: GCC O0/O2 compile/run 0; Clang O0/O2 compile 1, unknown builtins
    __builtin_isinff and __builtin_isinfl. EvoCC retains E2001 at __builtin_isinff.
  pr80692: GCC O0/O2 compile/run 0; Clang O0/O2 compile 1, unsupported _Decimal64
    and DD suffix. EvoCC retains E0112 at the decimal type declaration.
  pr85331: GCC O0/O2 compile/run 0; Clang O0/O2 compile 1, unknown builtin
    __builtin_shuffle and consequent int/vector type error. EvoCC retains
    E3050 for the floating vector. Integer shuffle support is not FP shuffle.
These are three distinct missing reference-language controls. Their original
sources/flags and oracle-unusable classification remain unchanged, not PASS.

Reproduce native controls in the sealed image:
  CC -std=gnu11 -O{0,2} -c hva-varargs-reference.c -o worker.o
  CC -std=gnu11 -O{0,2} -DHVA_DRIVER -DHVA_TRACE -c hva-varargs-reference.c -o driver.o
  gcc-14 worker.o driver.o -o probe; timeout 10 ./probe
Substitute exactly one object with EvoCC --target=aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu
--emit=asm output, assembled by GCC. Clang reference assembly uses Clang's
assembler because GNU as does not accept its .addrsig directive; no filtering.
Original torture: CC -std=gnu11 -O{0,2} ORIGINAL.c -lm -o probe; timeout 10 ./probe.

